<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi's Eastern Cement nine-month pre-tax rises.</title>
<headline>Saudi's Eastern Cement nine-month pre-tax rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(million Saudi riyals unless states)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	  217.8	    vs  200.4</p>
<p> Operating income	215.8	    vs  198.1</p>
<p> Costs			13.0	    vs   13.4</p>
<p> Other income	     15.0	    vs   15.7</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds     1.22 billion vs    1.16 billion.</p>
<p> Assets			1.28 billion vs    1.20 billion.</p>
<p>Full Name: The Eastern Province Cement Company.</p>
<p>Note: The Dammam-based firm, traded in the Saudi market, is one of eight cement companies in the kingdom.</p>
</text>
